Surface nature:  Pure PRESENTATIONAL, fully CONTROLLED primitive. The web source takes plain props (page,
                 pageSize, total, onPageChange, onPageSizeChange?, pageSizeOptions = [25,50,100]), derives a
                 little arithmetic (totalPages = max(1, ceil(total/pageSize)); start = (page-1)*pageSize+1;
                 end = min(page*pageSize, total)), and renders a <nav aria-label="Pagination"> pairing a
                 "Showing X–Y of Z" summary (+ an optional rows-per-page <select>) with a first / prev /
                 page-indicator / next / last button cluster. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, and
                 NO Promise — so it has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (nothing to fetch, fail,
                 age, or disconnect). Inventing such chrome would fabricate states the source does not have,
                 so this surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — the same faithful-parity stance
                 the sibling primitives ContextMenu (0206), DataTableColumnMenu (0210), and HelpTooltip
                 (0216) took. The REAL branches, all reproduced:
                   • empty        — total == 0 → "Showing 0–0 of 0" / "1 / 1" with every button disabled (a
                                    fully rendered control, NEVER a blank box).
                   • single-page  — total <= pageSize → totalPages == 1, all four buttons disabled.
                   • first page   — page == 1 of many → first/prev disabled (web `page <= 1`), next/last on.
                   • middle page  — all four navigation buttons enabled.
                   • last page    — page == totalPages → next/last disabled (web `page >= totalPages`).
                   • selector on  — onPageSizeChange supplied → rows-per-page Menu present; selector off when
                                    omitted (web `onPageSizeChange &&`); default and caller-supplied options.
                 Browser facilities map to native peers: lucide ChevronsLeft/ChevronLeft/ChevronRight/
                 ChevronsRight → layout-direction-aware SF Symbols chevron.backward.2 / chevron.backward /
                 chevron.forward / chevron.forward.2 (RTL-correct; the same names back SignalQueryControls);
                 the <select> → a SwiftUI Menu showing the current "N / page" with a checkmark on the
                 selected option; the `disabled:opacity-30` → `.opacity(0.3)` + `.disabled`; the
                 `flex-col sm:flex-row` responsive layout → ViewThatFits (single row when it fits, stacked
                 otherwise); `aria-live="polite"` on the showing summary → an AccessibilityNotification
                 .Announcement posted on change; the glyph scales with Dynamic Type via @ScaledMetric.

Data sources reproduced (from web source):
  • useTranslation                 -> PaginationStrings facade (P1/S10), table "Pagination"; every t() key
                                      routed through the injected PaginationResolve with i18next {{token}}
                                      interpolation (PaginationInterpolation).
  • props (page/pageSize/total/     -> PaginationController (@Observable @MainActor state-holder, P1/S8): it
    pageSizeOptions/onPageChange/      carries the controlled inputs (the parent mutates them, mirroring
    onPageSizeChange)                  React's controlled re-render), derives the PaginationProjection via
                                       the pure PaginationProjector, exposes every display + accessibility
                                       string, fires the navigation callbacks (gated by the disabled
                                       predicates), and emits the once-only view.opened (P1/S11).
  • body arithmetic                 -> PaginationProjector (Foundation-only, unit-tested): the verbatim port
                                       of totalPages / start / end and the `page <= 1` / `page >= totalPages`
                                       disabled predicates.

